<Concept title="HUmar saber Coliseum prototype" section="States">
<p>Issue #790: a scoped experiment in methodical combat. PSO animations provide the visual vocabulary; the rules below are provisional remake choices for owner playtesting, not verified PSO mechanics. This contract overrides ordinary player timing only in the explicitly enabled HUmar/saber Coliseum fixture.</p>
<ul>
<li>The prototype MUST use the current PSZ HUmar VRM and the complete mapped PSO saber set, source clips 097–111. Clips 112–113 belong to sword. Utility clips remain available for inspection even when the encounter does not invoke them.</li>
<li>A living nearby enemy within 6 metres MUST keep locomotion in caution walk; leaving that range MUST restore ordinary walk-to-run progression. Fixed player/enemy levels MUST make repeated encounters comparable.</li>
<li>An idle or walking Hunter facing an incoming melee attacker within a 60-degree half-angle MAY automatically guard. Attacking, running, rolling, frozen, recovering, defeated or menu-blocked players MUST NOT start a guard. Guard MUST absorb one physical hit, play the block clip and commit the player until its end. This is deterministic experimental defense, not a stat-based PSO evasion formula.</li>
<li>Guard MUST NOT cancel an attack or cure status effects. Status ticks, ranged attacks and rear hits MUST retain ordinary damage handling. A successful guard MUST NOT award damage-based Photon Blast charge.</li>
<li>PSO saber swings MUST use their own provisional contact fractions (0.40, 0.40, 0.45), with one contact event per step. Chain input MUST use the prototype window 0.55–0.95, preserve single-slot queuing and commitment, and have no timing damage bonus. These values MUST be visually checked and tuned with owner feedback.</li>
<li>The experiment MUST NOT change campaign, other weapons/classes, EXP, status semantics or global enemy resources. Existing enemy behavior is the baseline; adjust only demonstrated obstacles to this test.</li>
</ul>
<p>Verification requires deterministic guard boundaries and live real-rig checks of all 15 clips, locomotion, attack contact, guard, interruption and recovery. Owner review determines whether the exchange feels fair; passing checks does not raise the Combat or Character grades. Status redesign remains separate in #789.</p>
</Concept>
